{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543","id":6052076342,"node_id":"I_kwDONuYWx88AAAABaLtbNg","number":543,"title":"`coin_flip`: the constant answer \"0\" receives full reward","user":{"login":"maximusrufus","id":14168894,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTY4ODk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14168894?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus","html_url":"https://github.com/maximusrufus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximusrufus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-27T03:01:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T03:01:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In `reasoning_gym/probability/coin_flip.py` (lines 139-147 at 49b0713), `score_answer` gives prefix credit `match_len / min(len(answer), len(oracle))`. For the answer `\"0\"` and an oracle such as `\"0.875\"`, this is 1/1, so the score is 1.0.\n\nReproduction (seed 42, 8 instances): the answer `\"0\"` scores 1.0 on 7 of 8; the exception is the instance whose answer is exactly `\"1\"`.\n\n```python\nimport reasoning_gym\nds = reasoning_gym.create_dataset(\"coin_flip\", seed=42, size=8)\nprint([ds.score_answer(\"0\", entry=e) for e in ds])\n```\n\nAny prefix of the oracle also scores 1.0 (for example `\"0.8\"` or `\"0.87\"` for 0.875), so a policy trained on this task could learn to answer \"0\". Dividing by the oracle string's length instead of the shorter of the two would stop a short prefix from scoring 1.0; partial credit could also be based on numeric error.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/543/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}